project KSHIAI_BATTLE_PIPELINE_REVISION_POC:
  version 6
  title "Evidence-driven PoC for the purpose-scoped canonical battle pipeline"
  description |
    Evaluate the interventions proposed by
    docs/battle-pipeline-revised-design.md without assuming that the final battle
    result is objectively correct. Freeze a baseline and evaluation protocol,
    build the minimum reversible prototype for each intervention, compare it
    against the baseline, and record supported revise unsupported or
    indeterminate. Hard invariants such as authority privacy atomicity and schema
    validity remain pass or fail requirements; outcome plausibility coherence
    causal traceability and efficiency are proxy evidence rather than proof.
    The DAG is a candidate sequence only. Each later PoC entry task is initially
    blocked as a decision lock. A supported evaluation permits an explicit
    unblock; revise unsupported or indeterminate requires an explicit replan.
    No milestone in this PoC authorizes production persistence migration
    provider-order changes release deployment or legacy cleanup.
  as_of 2026-08-06
  duration_unit point
  velocity 9p/4d
  finish POC_EVIDENCE_REVIEWED

resource DEV:
  title "Developer"
  capacity 1

milestone CURRENT_PIPELINE:
  title "Existing battle pipeline available as the comparison subject"
  state reached

milestone DESIGN_FIXED:
  title "Revised battle-pipeline hypotheses and authority boundaries fixed"
  state reached

milestone BASELINE_READY:
  title "Frozen scenarios metrics thresholds and current-pipeline baseline ready"
  state reached

milestone PROJECTION_POC_BUILT:
  title "Purpose-specific projection prototype built behind a PoC boundary"
  state reached

milestone PROJECTION_EVALUATED:
  title "Projection effectiveness and failure modes evaluated"
  state reached

milestone PROJECTION_REVISION_POC_BUILT:
  title "Server-side projection revision prototype built"
  state reached

milestone PROJECTION_REVISION_EVALUATED:
  title "Projection revision evaluated against the frozen protocol"
  state reached

milestone PATCH_POC_BUILT:
  title "Bounded canonical-patch prototype built in shadow mode"
  state reached

milestone PATCH_EVALUATED:
  title "Canonical-patch effectiveness and failure modes evaluated"
  state reached

milestone ISSUES_POC_BUILT:
  title "Consistency-issue lifecycle prototype built without canonical mutation authority"
  state reached

milestone ISSUES_EVALUATED:
  title "Consistency-issue effectiveness and failure modes evaluated"
  state reached

milestone READ_COHERENCE_POC_BUILT:
  title "Purpose-scoped read and bounded-repair prototype built"
  state reached

milestone READ_COHERENCE_EVALUATED:
  title "Read-time coherence and repair effectiveness evaluated"

milestone GRAPH_POC_BUILT:
  title "In-memory canonical graph view prototype built over BattleState"

milestone GRAPH_EVALUATED:
  title "Canonical graph projection value and migration risk evaluated"

milestone ADAPTIVE_POC_BUILT:
  title "Fast coarse and selective-expansion adjudication prototype built"

milestone ADAPTIVE_EVALUATED:
  title "Adaptive adjudication quality and cost effectiveness evaluated"

milestone WORLD_PROCESS_POC_BUILT:
  title "Rule-based active world-process prototype built in the shared timeline"

milestone WORLD_PROCESS_EVALUATED:
  title "World-process integration effectiveness and failure modes evaluated"

milestone POC_EVIDENCE_REVIEWED:
  title "PoC evidence limitations and next decisions recorded"

task T_DESIGN CURRENT_PIPELINE -> DESIGN_FIXED:
  title "Freeze revised pipeline principles contracts and PoC authority boundary"
  description |
    Record the design hypotheses and preserve the existing BattleState
    perception narration timing provider and release authority boundaries.
    State explicitly that canonical commit is adoption rather than a proof of
    global consistency and that the PoC cannot prove an objectively correct
    final battle result.
  duration 1p
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_BASELINE DESIGN_FIXED -> BASELINE_READY:
  title "Pre-register the PoC corpus metrics thresholds and baseline"
  description |
    Freeze representative ordinary ambiguous contradictory remote-interaction
    simultaneous irreversible world-process legacy and provider-failure
    scenarios before inspecting prototype output. Record current-pipeline
    outputs repeated-run variance LLM calls tokens latency state size slice size
    known-fact contradictions unsupported claims causal gaps and human-rubric
    plausibility. Separate hard invariants from proxy quality measures. Define
    sample counts reviewer blinding comparison method minimum material effect
    thresholds stop conditions and the supported revise unsupported and
    indeterminate decision rubric. Hash or otherwise freeze fixtures and scoring
    inputs so later phases cannot silently move the baseline.
  duration 2p
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_PROJECTION_POC BASELINE_READY -> PROJECTION_POC_BUILT:
  title "Prototype bounded purpose-specific slices over current BattleState"
  description |
    Implement the minimum InteractionScope ObservationSlice AdjudicationSlice
    ConsistencySlice and CanonicalReadResult adapters needed by the frozen
    scenarios. Keep the prototype read-only and do not change battle outcomes.
    Include physical remote causal support communication identity and
    world-process traversal, observer-local references, and configurable fact
    entity rule byte and history limits.
  duration 2p
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_PROJECTION_EVAL PROJECTION_POC_BUILT -> PROJECTION_EVALUATED:
  title "Measure projection relevance reduction leakage and missed dependencies"
  description |
    Compare each slice with the frozen baseline and seeded ground-truth
    interaction fixtures. Measure decisive-fact recall irrelevant-fact reduction
    prompt bytes and token estimate latency bound compliance A/B isolation
    canonical-ID leakage and unchanged baseline outcomes. Probe false negatives
    with remote targeting support propagation communication and identity
    mutations. Record supported revise unsupported or indeterminate with failure
    examples and uncertainty. Do not proceed automatically unless the evidence
    supports a useful bounded projection contract.
  duration 1p
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_PROJECTION_REVISION_POC PROJECTION_EVALUATED -> PROJECTION_REVISION_POC_BUILT:
  title "Revise server-side projection compactness without weakening recall"
  description |
    Keep the ObservationSlice boundary and all read-only authority privacy and
    unchanged-outcome invariants. Revise only the server-side adjudication and
    consistency representations by deduplicating overlapping world semantic and
    mechanical claims and using compact purpose-specific DTOs. Preserve anchor
    relation active-process and recent-causal recall. Do not alter the frozen
    fixture decision rubric or thresholds, and do not start canonical patches.
  duration 2p
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_PROJECTION_REVISION_EVAL PROJECTION_REVISION_POC_BUILT -> PROJECTION_REVISION_EVALUATED:
  title "Re-evaluate the projection revision with the unchanged protocol"
  description |
    Re-run the same frozen fixture and 20-repetition protocol. Require zero hard
    invariant failures decisive-fact recall of at least 0.98 weighted byte
    reduction of at least 0.30 p95 latency no greater than 25 milliseconds and
    unchanged baseline outcomes. Record supported revise unsupported or
    indeterminate. Use XAI only for an actual unresolved semantic ambiguity; it
    cannot offset a deterministic metric failure. Do not proceed automatically
    unless the result is supported.
  duration 1p
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_PATCH_POC PROJECTION_REVISION_EVALUATED -> PATCH_POC_BUILT:
  title "Prototype authority-preserving canonical patches in shadow mode"
  description |
    Add minimal CanonicalFact provenance validity CausalLink assertion
    retraction touched-reference and patch-audit contracts. Convert selected
    existing mechanical semantic free-action and world transitions without
    making the patch path authoritative. Run schema reference direct-conflict
    forbidden-state retraction causal revision and size checks while preserving
    existing subsystem authority and atomic commit behavior.
  duration 2p
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_PATCH_EVAL PATCH_POC_BUILT -> PATCH_EVALUATED:
  title "Measure patch parity audit yield scope reduction and false rejection"
  description |
    Shadow-compare reconstructed post-state touched references and causal sources
    with the existing authoritative result. Measure conversion parity invalid
    patch detection seeded-defect recall false rejection audit scope size and
    unexplained state changes. Confirm that no converted patch can cross
    mechanical semantic perception narration or private-state authority. Record
    supported revise unsupported or indeterminate and stop for unexplained
    parity drift or authority regression.
  duration 1p
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_ISSUES_POC PATCH_EVALUATED -> ISSUES_POC_BUILT:
  title "Prototype consistency issue registration and purpose blocking"
  description |
    Implement the minimum strict issue alert and audit-result contracts plus
    deterministic registration deduplication defer and resolve operations.
    Store the prototype in a reversible PoC envelope. LLM alerts may propose an
    issue but may not alter canonical state. Keep no_issue_found scoped and
    indeterminate distinct from success.
  duration 1p
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_ISSUES_EVAL ISSUES_POC_BUILT -> ISSUES_EVALUATED:
  title "Measure issue detection actionability noise and lifecycle correctness"
  description |
    Seed direct subtle unrelated duplicate stale deferred and newly discovered
    conflicts. Measure detection recall false positive rate deduplication
    stability purpose-blocking classification lifecycle traceability storage
    growth and operator-review burden. Verify that unrelated issues do not block
    a usable purpose slice and that nondeferred state is never labeled globally
    coherent. Record supported revise unsupported or indeterminate.
  duration 1p
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_READ_POC ISSUES_EVALUATED -> READ_COHERENCE_POC_BUILT:
  title "Prototype local read checks and bounded repair strategies"
  description |
    Run cheap checks over complete purpose slices and return exact checked facts
    and unresolved issues. Prototype select reinterpret intermediate-state
    weaken-claim and reset-unknown repair behind a nonproduction flag. Emit
    repairs as ordinary RepairRef patches, preserve causal and authority order,
    rebuild the slice, and cap attempts calls and touched facts.
  duration 2p
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_READ_EVAL READ_COHERENCE_POC_BUILT -> READ_COHERENCE_EVALUATED:
  title "Measure local coherence gain repair harm and graceful degradation"
  description |
    Compare conflict visibility before and after the PoC on frozen and adversarial
    cases. Measure blocking-conflict reduction successful coherent reads
    incorrect fact selection causal regression unnecessary repair unknown
    fallback rate extra LLM calls latency and repeated-repair loops. Require no
    mutation outside the checked scope and no rewrite of public history. Record
    supported revise unsupported or indeterminate; an apparently coherent but
    causally weaker result counts as harm rather than success.
  duration 1p
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_GRAPH_POC READ_COHERENCE_EVALUATED -> GRAPH_POC_BUILT:
  title "Prototype an in-memory canonical graph view over legacy BattleState"
  description |
    Build indexed entity fact temporal causal world-process issue and rule
    access over the current JSON without changing persistence authority. Exercise
    projection and patch reads through the graph adapter, keep deterministic
    legacy reconstruction, and add a disposable persistence-envelope experiment
    only if restart measurement requires it. Do not backfill production data or
    remove existing fields.
  duration 2p
  status blocked
  blocked_reason "Unblock only after read-coherence evidence supports continuation; otherwise replan"
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_GRAPH_EVAL GRAPH_POC_BUILT -> GRAPH_EVALUATED:
  title "Measure graph query value parity complexity and migration risk"
  description |
    Compare graph and direct-adapter projections for fact equality order
    independence and committed-outcome parity. Measure scope-query latency
    memory serialized growth index maintenance reconstruction and restart cost
    implementation complexity and rollback behavior. Identify which graph
    components provide material value and which should remain derived views.
    Record supported revise unsupported or indeterminate without treating faster
    queries alone as proof that independent persistence is warranted.
  duration 2p
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_ADAPTIVE_POC GRAPH_EVALUATED -> ADAPTIVE_POC_BUILT:
  title "Prototype fast coarse and selectively expanded adjudication"
  description |
    Route only frozen PoC scenarios through deterministic Level 0 bounded Level 1
    and explicitly triggered Level 2 paths. Keep existing resolution as control.
    Expand plans from the character observation psychology experience and intent
    without adjudicator-invented tactics. Refine unknown facts without replacing
    known facts, execute the longest valid prefix, derive costs from completed
    execution, enforce per-purpose budgets, and degrade unsupported detail toward
    intermediate weak or unknown states.
  duration 3p
  status blocked
  blocked_reason "Unblock only after graph evidence supports continuation; otherwise replan"
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_ADAPTIVE_EVAL ADAPTIVE_POC_BUILT -> ADAPTIVE_EVALUATED:
  title "Measure adjudication plausibility detail value cost and regression"
  description |
    Use repeated runs and blinded pairwise rubric review because no objective
    final-result oracle exists. Measure preference and explanation scores
    known-fact contradiction unsupported assertion causal trace completeness
    expansion trigger precision and recall partial-prefix correctness fast-path
    outcome parity calls tokens latency and budget degradation. Report hard
    invariant failures separately from proxy quality improvements. Record
    supported revise unsupported or indeterminate and retain raw scenario-level
    evidence for later review.
  duration 2p
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_WORLD_POC ADAPTIVE_EVALUATED -> WORLD_PROCESS_POC_BUILT:
  title "Prototype active world proposals in the shared temporal window"
  description |
    Implement rule-based examples for fire collapse fall spread and support loss
    with source trigger effect and timing references. Place them beside character
    proposals in the existing side-neutral temporal resolver and route results
    through the PoC execution patch and projection path. Use semantic expansion
    only for a frozen ambiguous fixture and keep the feature disabled outside the
    PoC harness.
  duration 2p
  status blocked
  blocked_reason "Unblock only after adaptive-adjudication evidence supports continuation; otherwise replan"
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_WORLD_EVAL WORLD_PROCESS_POC_BUILT -> WORLD_PROCESS_EVALUATED:
  title "Measure environmental continuity interaction quality cost and side neutrality"
  description |
    Measure expected process progression trigger and propagation coverage
    character-process conflict handling causal completeness human-rubric
    plausibility A/B swap symmetry same-bucket atomicity terminal behavior extra
    calls latency and unsupported environmental inventions. Compare with the
    no-active-process baseline and record supported revise unsupported or
    indeterminate.
  duration 1p
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_SYNTHESIS WORLD_PROCESS_EVALUATED -> POC_EVIDENCE_REVIEWED:
  title "Synthesize intervention evidence limitations and next decisions"
  description |
    Publish a matrix for every intervention containing hypothesis prototype
    scope baseline metrics observed effect uncertainty failure modes hard
    invariant result decision and recommended next experiment. Separate local
    improvements from interaction effects and identify measurements invalidated
    by earlier revisions. Conclude only whether each intervention is supported
    for further engineering revised rejected or still indeterminate. Do not claim
    objective battle correctness global consistency production readiness or
    release acceptance. Run focused harness tests full repository regression
    checks static privacy and authority audits and PERT validation, while keeping
    any implementation migration release and production plan separately gated.
  duration 2p
  requires:
    DEV 1
